    "result_text": "The JDBC repo uses `SimpleJdbcInsert` with `BeanPropertySqlParameterSource`, so it auto-maps the new `title` bean property \u2014 no change needed there (its partial SELECTs are a pre-existing legacy shape, and the active test profile is `spring-data-jpa`/Hibernate anyway).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature end-to-end. The endpoint is the single black-box path `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}`, wired through OfficeFloor functions, so `title` had to persist for the GET to reproduce the salutation.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (DTOs are generated from this):\n   - Added `title` to the `OwnerFields` input schema (optional string, `^(MR|MRS|MS|DR)$`).\n   - Added `salutation` as a read-only field on the `Owner` output schema.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps `title` in both directions (request\u2192entity, entity\u2192DTO) since it's a plain `String` on both sides.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `salutation` mapping expression: `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present, else just `lastName`.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `title` column so the JPA/Hibernate persistence round-trips it.\n\nI chose a plain-string `title` over an OpenAPI `enum` deliberately: an enum would generate a `TitleEnum` type, forcing awkward enum\u2194`String` MapStruct conversions against the JPA entity, whereas plain strings match the codebase's established pattern (locality, etc.).\n\nThe full test suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`, which asserts `salutation == \"DR who\"` for `title=DR`/`lastName=who`) is green: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
