    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change follows the existing conventions of this codebase cleanly:\n\n- **Right unit.** The `salutation` is a derived, read-only display field computed from the entity \u2014 exactly what the neighboring `displayName` and `initials` `@Mapping` expressions in `OwnerMapper` already are. Placing it there sits it next to its peers rather than scattering derived-field logic across the entity or a new class. A maintainer would look here first.\n- **No duplication / no catch-all.** `OwnerMapper` is already the home for these owner-response derivations, so adding one more is additive, not a new responsibility bolted onto an unrelated class. The `title` field/getter/setter on `Owner` mirrors the existing `address`/`Person` field style.\n- **Consistent, complete edges.** The new column is added to all four dialect schemas (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres) in the same position, and both the request (`title`) and response (`salutation`) sides are documented in `openapi.yml` with matching descriptions and a `pattern` constraint reflecting the spec's allowed titles. Nothing is left half-wired.\n- **Spec alignment in the natural idiom.** The null/blank ternary yielding `title + \" \" + lastName` else `lastName` matches the spec, and expressing it inline as a MapStruct expression matches how `displayName`/`initials` handle the same kind of conditional-free/derived logic.\n\nNo structural changes needed.",
